          %h3#AsFibrationsInCanonicalModelStructures As fibrations in canonical model structures
          %p
            The isofibrations are the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+categories"} canonical model structure on categories
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+groupoids"} canonical model structure on groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structures"} canonical model structures
            on various types of higher categories are usually some generalization of isofibrations. For example, the fibrations in the Lack model structure on 2-Cat, known as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifibrations"} equifibrations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasicategories
            have “equivalence lifting” at all levels.
          %p
            Generalizing in another direction, internalized isofibrations are the fibrations in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-trivial+model+structure"} 2-trivial model structure
            on any finitely complete and cocomplete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amnestic+isofibration"} amnestic isofibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isocofibration"} isocofibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifibration"} equifibration
          %h2#references References
          %p For groupoids the definition appears (called “star surjectivity” there) on p. 105 (3 of 30) in
          %ul
            %li#Brown70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fibrations of groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693%2870%2990089-X"} 10.1016/0021-8693(70)90089-X
              %a{:href => "http://groupoids.org.uk/pdffiles/fibrationsgpds.pdf"} author’s pdf
